    <DataNode elementId="AT3G02870-MONOMER" textLabel="L-galactose-1-phosphate phosphatase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9M8S8" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The enzyme was partially purified from Arabidopsis shoots. The enzyme has an absolute dependency on Mg2+. The corresponding gene was identified to be AT3G02870. Mutant plants show a 50% reduction of total ascorbate concentration. Recombinant VTC4 (At3g02870) was shown a multi-functional enzyme. In addition to L-galactose 1-phosphate, both D-myo-inositol 3-phosphate and D-myo-inositol 1-phosphate are also good substrates of the recombinant protein |CITS: [19339506]|.</Comment>
